# Fast loading UI (must)

Optimize perceived and real load on every landing. Target Lighthouse performance-friendly patterns.

## LCP / above the fold

1. Only **hero** critical media + navbar logo get `priority` / high fetch
2. Do **not** set `priority` on product/testimonial cards below the fold
3. Hero: one dominant image; prefer `.webp` from the asset pack
4. Header logo: `priority` OK (small)

## Images

- `next/image` with correct `sizes`
- `next.config`: `formats: ["image/avif", "image/webp"]`, sensible `deviceSizes`
- **`images.qualities`**: include every `quality={N}` used (e.g. `[60, 65, 75]`) or console spam
- Logo CSS height only → `style={{ width: "auto" }}`
- Prefer pack webp; transparent PNG only when needed
- Tiny favicons (`favicon-brand.mdc`) - never 1MB logo as icon

## Fonts

- `next/font` with `display: "swap"`
- Load **minimal weights** (e.g. body 400/600/700/800; skip unused 500)
- Script/display fonts: `preload: false` if not LCP text

## JS / sections

- Keep Hero + Header eagerly imported
- **Dynamic import** below-fold sections (`Science` → `Footer`) via `next/dynamic`
- `optimizePackageImports` for `lucide-react`, `motion`, `swiper` when used
- `"use client"` only where needed

## Config

```ts
// next.config.ts
poweredByHeader: false
compress: true
images: {
  formats: ["image/avif", "image/webp"],
  qualities: [60, 65, 75],
}
```

## Checklist

- [ ] One LCP image strategy (hero)
- [ ] Fonts swap + fewer weights
- [ ] Below-fold dynamic imports
- [ ] Image formats AVIF/WebP enabled
- [ ] `images.qualities` matches usage
- [ ] No giant favicon; transparent pad
- [ ] `npm run build` green